{:db/id 17592186100992 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186100687 :question/id #uuid "1b15db42-aba2-575c-a01e-b715450329fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4379" :question/problem "Find $A+C-(B+A),$ if\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C-(B+A) & =A+C-B-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{A}+C-B-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C-B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-3 & -1-(-1) \\\\ 1-2 & 2-0 \\\\ -6-(-4) & 1-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e62b0e-adda-5d35-aeb9-961057dce8f0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049939}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186101130 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7de1032-850c-5ea9-a1ae-e083486ff706" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186098116} {:answer/id #uuid "ee11b057-083a-50d4-a16e-71b940dfbd15" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186098117} {:answer/id #uuid "ee16e495-0276-53ba-a14b-1b616dfd5ae4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186098118} {:answer/id #uuid "f6f5f24e-1c43-5e7d-b296-3a57df79f5fe" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatri